[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A socket under .devenv exceeds the sockaddr cap for most worktrees

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[EVIDENCE]
UID: EV-SCRIBE-SOCKET-PATH-LENGTHS
TITLE: A socket under .devenv exceeds the sockaddr cap for most worktrees
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
SOURCE: 27 registered worktrees on the operator's machine; 104-byte cap; 2026-08-31
STATEMENT: >>>
Socket path lengths measured across the 27 worktrees registered on the
operator's machine, against the 104-byte sockaddr_un cap the reference
implementation enforces.

Under <worktree>/.devenv/state/, 24 of 27 exceed the cap. The longest real
worktree reaches 130 bytes and the strictdoc-trial worktree itself is 106.
Only the primary checkout (80) and two short slugs (99, 101) fit.

Under the user runtime directory every scheme fits: a sanitized basename is 33
to 58 bytes, a sanitized branch name 29 to 62, and a hash a constant 45.
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is set to /run/user/1000, mode 0700, owned by the user, on
tmpfs, and removed by pam_systemd at final logout.

Identity: a resolved absolute path is the only stable key. A branch name is
empty or literally HEAD on a detached worktree, one of which exists here, and
one worktree already deviates from the flat-slug convention with a nested
directory component.
<<<
